<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Good rains had alleviated in part dryness in Cordoba and Santa Fe provinces by September 27, the Agriculture Secretariat said Thursday in its weekly crop report.</p>
<p>The rain allowed maize sowing to restart in Cordoba and Chaco provinces. Farmers throughout Argentina have now planted 9.8 percent of total maize intentions. Sunflower sowing reached 3.7 percent. Wheat is in mainly good shape. But the crop needed more rain in parts of northeast Buenos Aires, northern La Pampa, and parts of Cordoba, Santa Fe and Entre Rios.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets). Yield in quintals per hectare.</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..................Yield</p>
<p> Wheat     6,828  100.0(100.0)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Maize     3,779    9.8  (8.4)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Soybeans    n/a    n/a  (n/a)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sunflower 2,980    3.7  (2.0)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sorghum     n/a    n/a  (n/a)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Cotton	n/a    n/a  (n/a)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p>-- Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541-318-0655</p>
